From ce5a792c0d49e7b5becc0178599bcfa8a55802bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gambhiro <gambhiro@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 20:38:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Android: [DEBUG, DO NOT MERGE] log IME calls under the
 QtThaiDbg tag

Temporary instrumentation for investigating the lost one-shot Shift of
Gboard's Thai layout. Every line uses the logcat tag QtThaiDbg and
starts with a sequence number (seq=jN on the Java side, seq=cN in C++).

Java:
- QtInputConnection: every InputConnection method the IME calls, with
  arguments and result; for getExtractedText also the request token,
  flags and GET_EXTRACTED_TEXT_MONITOR; for finishComposingText whether
  the IME called it or Qt's own sendKeyEvent. Also logs (and passes on
  to BaseInputConnection) requestCursorUpdates, performEditorAction,
  clearMetaKeyStates, deleteSurroundingTextInCodePoints,
  getSurroundingText and closeConnection, which Qt does not override.
- QtEditText: onCreateInputConnection (EditorInfo fields),
  onCheckIsTextEditor, onKeyDown, onKeyUp.
- QtInputDelegate: every InputMethodManager and WindowInsetsController
  call (updateSelection, restartInput, showSoftInput, show/hide(ime),
  hideSoftInputFromWindow), showSoftwareKeyboard, onKeyDown, onKeyUp.

C++ (only where qt.qpa.input.methods logging has no line):
- getCursorCapsMode result,
- focusObjectStopComposing when it commits a preedit,
- showInputPanel, with the focus object's class,
- the key events passed to QWindowSystemInterface.
